<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-Bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-Bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 8.958 percent at Wednesday's auction from 8.940 percent at the previous auction on June 11.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 1.2 billion pounds and accepted bids for 1,330.525 million. Bills worth 761.750 million pounds mature on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Sept 18, 1997 (Sept 11, 1997).</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.958 percent (8.940).</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,330.525 million (1,458.775 million).</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,705.525 million (1,535.825 million).</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.600 - 9.023 percent (8.499 - 9.006).</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.600 - 10.099 percent (8.499 - 10.099).</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 88 (110).</p>
<p>Number of bids: 92 (115).</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
